# Caddy's global options on a machine served through a Cloudflare Tunnel, laid
# by `sitesolide setup --tunnel` at /etc/caddy/global.d/tunnel.caddy, which the
# global block of infra/caddy/Caddyfile imports. See docs/tunnel.md.
#
# Behind the tunnel every request reaches Caddy from cloudflared, over the
# loopback, and the visitor's address is in Cf-Connecting-Ip, which
# Cloudflare's edge sets on every request it hands the tunnel. Trusting ::1,
# where the connector reaches Caddy, and that header from it alone, makes that
# address {client_ip}, which every generated block hands its app as
# X-Forwarded-For (bin/cli/fragment.ts). Without it, every visitor reaches
# every app as the loopback: one visitor in the analytics, and the dashboard's
# limiter of failed attempts shared by the whole Internet.
#
# ::1 alone, never 127.0.0.1: the monitor's and the gatekeeper's probes reach
# Caddy there, and so can any project's service, which would then be counted
# as any visitor it names. The loopback rule keeps ::1 to the connector's
# account (bin/cli/loopback.ts). A request from anywhere else keeps its peer's
# address, whatever header it carries.
servers {
	trusted_proxies static ::1/128
	client_ip_headers Cf-Connecting-Ip
}
